A band's S50 pools its << F.g4_n_focal_events_per_band >> focal events, the morphologies over its << F.g4_locations_per_band >> locations; patch events enter neither S50 nor the paired tests. The paired ratio S50\textsubscript{Neuromag}/S50\textsubscript{OPM} is above 1 when the OPM array needs less strength (Section~\ref{sec:S1}), and interval bounds printed as 1.00 are classed by their unrounded values throughout. The adult sat at its measured pose and the smaller heads at top contact (main text, Section 2.5), so the adult's spike results are not placed by the same rule as theirs.

The exploratory spike endpoint, chosen after the analyses (Section~\ref{sec:S8.2}), was the dense array against Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels in the << F.g4_band_10_20mm >> mm band with the practical detector. It was tested with the two-sided exact sign-flip test on per-location differences in detection counts, Holm-adjusted \citep{holm1979} over the << F.g4_n_anatomies >> anatomies, with the paired S50 ratio and its location-bootstrap interval as the effect size. This band, array and detector were chosen from the << F.g4_family_per_opm_array >> comparisons per OPM array of each anatomy, a selection that the correction over anatomies does not control. The detection family has << F.g4_family_per_anatomy >> comparisons per anatomy: two OPM arrays against Neuromag's << F.g2_squid_channels >> channels, its gradiometers and its magnetometers, with both detectors, in << F.g4_n_depth_bands >> depth bands. The localization family has << F.loc_family_per_anatomy >> comparisons per anatomy: two OPM arrays, focal and patch sources at two strengths, and the endpoints. These are the dipole error, the two errors of dynamic statistical parametric mapping (dSPM), and joint detection and localization with the study's dSPM or with the dipole.

The sign-flip test uses the locations whose difference in detection counts is not zero, and p is smallest when all of them favor one array. With a band's << F.meth_locs_per_band >> locations that smallest p is << F.meth_signflip_min_p_18 >>, and p < << F.meth_alpha >> needs at least << F.meth_signflip_min_n >> such locations. With equal differences the test is the exact sign test. Of << F.meth_locs_per_band >> locations, << F.meth_signtest_18_k >> must then favor one array for p < << F.meth_alpha >> (p = << F.meth_signtest_18_k_p >>; with << F.meth_signtest_18_kminus1 >>, p = << F.meth_signtest_18_kminus1_p >>), and << F.meth_signtest_18_k_holm >> for the first Holm step over << F.meth_n_anatomies >> anatomies, p < << F.meth_holm_first_alpha >> (p = << F.meth_signtest_18_k_holm_p >>). Of the pre-specified << F.meth_confirm_locs >> locations (<< F.meth_confirm_locs_per_stratum >> per orientation stratum), << F.meth_signtest_36_k >> are needed (p = << F.meth_signtest_36_k_p >>) and << F.meth_signtest_36_k_holm >> for the first Holm step (p = << F.meth_signtest_36_k_holm_p >>).

Unequal differences can move p either way: the adult's << F.meth_adult_locs_opm >> locations favoring the OPM against << F.meth_adult_locs_squid >> favoring Neuromag gave p = << F.meth_adult_p >>, against << F.meth_adult_equal_p >> had the differences been equal. Beyond << F.meth_signflip_exact_max >> non-zero locations the run estimated p from << F.meth_signflip_mc_patterns >> random sign patterns (resolution << F.meth_signflip_mc_resolution >>); the p values reported for the pre-specified run are exact (Section~\ref{sec:S7.5}). These values follow from the design alone; power and a minimal detectable S50 ratio depend on how detection varies between locations and were not computed. The pilot runs that preceded the pre-specified run (Section~\ref{sec:S8.2}) do not estimate power either.

\subsection{Results of the exploratory run}\label{sec:S7.2}

The exploratory run had one noise realization per event and an endpoint chosen after the analyses; it is superseded as evidence by the pre-specified run (main text, Section 3.6; Section~\ref{sec:S7.5}). Here and in Section~\ref{sec:S7.5}, counts and ranges over the anatomies include the << F.g3b_infant18mo_age_months >>-month template and the << F.wr_n_children_words >> school-aged children, which the main text reports separately (Section~\ref{sec:S10}). Every anatomy's S50 point estimate favored the dense array << F.g4_band_10_20mm >> mm below the scalp (Fig.~\ref{fig:S12}A; Table~\ref{tab:S10}). So did the per-location counts under a Holm correction over the << F.g4_n_anatomies >> anatomies (largest adjusted p << F.g4_holm_10_20mm_max_p_adj >>, child A, whose S50 interval spans 1). The anatomies are not independent replications.

Table~\ref{tab:S10} sets the oracle's S50 ratio, the quantity most directly tied to the detectability metric, beside the practical detector's. The oracle's ratios were the larger in << F.wr_g4_oracle_above_practical_n >> of the << F.g4_n_anatomies >> anatomies (not in the << F.wr_g4_oracle_below_practical_heads >>), as expected where the oracle's advantage is not diluted by the scan over times and candidates. The adult's detection curves are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:S13}.

