\subsection{Localization}\label{sec:S7.3}

Localization was examined at << F.loc_n_locations >> locations with focal and patch sources of << F.loc_strengths_nam >> nAm, one event per source type and strength at each location (<< F.loc_events_per_condition >> per condition, unstretched morphology), in independent null data. The inverse used a single-compartment boundary-element model (BEM), whereas the simulation used three layers. Each location's inverse also carried one of << F.loc_coreg_draws >> coregistration-error draws of << F.loc_coreg_shift_mm >> mm and << F.loc_coreg_angle_deg >>°, the same for every array. This error displaced the adult's sources by a median of << F.loc_adult_coreg_displacement_mm >> mm, and by << F.loc_coreg_displacement_mm_range >> mm over the anatomies. The noise covariance was a Ledoit--Wolf estimate from << F.loc_baseline_minutes >> min of null data. The source grid had fixed orientations at << F.loc_grid_spacing_mm >>-mm spacing (<< F.loc_inverse_grid_range >> sources) and excluded the true source vertices.

Equivalent current dipoles (ECDs) were fitted with MNE-Python \citep{gramfort2013} at least << F.loc_ecd_min_dist_mm >> mm inside the inner skull. dSPM \citep{dale2000}, with depth weighting << F.loc_depth_weighting >> and a regularization set by an assumed signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) of << F.loc_snr >>, was computed in the study's implementation and in MNE-Python's, at the true peak sample. The error is the distance from the true source (a patch's center) to the dipole or to the dSPM peak, read on the MRI through the perturbed transform. Joint success is detection by the practical detector (thresholds for << F.g4_operating_point_per_minute >> false event per minute from << F.loc_calibration_minutes >> min of null data) with an error of at most << F.loc_joint_threshold_mm >> mm. Paired error differences were tested with the Wilcoxon signed-rank test and joint success with an exact McNemar test.

Both dSPM implementations use fixed orientations on the same grid, the same noise covariance, a depth exponent of << F.meth_dspm_depth >>, $\lambda^{2}$ = << F.meth_dspm_lambda2 >>, a source covariance scaled to the whitened rank and dSPM normalization. They differ in the depth weighting. The study's implementation uses the whitened gains of all of an array's channels, without a limit. MNE-Python's is limited at its default of << F.meth_mne_depth_limit >> and uses the unwhitened gains of the gradiometers, or of the magnetometers where there are none (the OPM arrays). Both are reported, because the paired dSPM differences depend on this choice.

Dipole fits of detected << F.loc_strength_high_nam >>-nAm focal spikes had median errors of << F.loc_ecd_det_focal320_mm_range >> mm in every array and anatomy. The errors include every event, detected or not, because selecting on detection would select on each system's own noise. At << F.loc_strength_low_nam >> nAm, all << F.wr_locfig_n_open_80nam >> estimates of Fig.~\ref{fig:S14} rest mostly on undetected events, whose errors are those of noise. Of the << F.wr_locfig_n_error_comparisons >> median error differences, << F.wr_locfig_n_zero_median >> were exactly zero, because the dSPM peaks of both systems often fall on the same vertex of the shared << F.loc_grid_spacing_mm >>-mm grid, and << F.wr_locfig_n_positive_median >> were positive (Neuromag closer).

The localization family holds << F.loc_family_n >> paired comparisons: the << F.wr_locfig_n_error_comparisons >> error differences of Fig.~\ref{fig:S14} (Wilcoxon signed-rank tests) and << F.wr_jointfig_n_mcnemar_per_method >> joint-success comparisons each for the dipole fit and the study's dSPM (exact McNemar tests; Fig.~\ref{fig:S15}). Of the << F.loc_family_n >>, << F.loc_family_n_sig >> had p < << F.wr_p_exploratory_threshold >>, where << F.loc_family_expected_by_chance >> would be expected by chance. Among the error differences these were << F.loc_family_n_sig_ecd >> for the dipole fit, << F.loc_family_n_sig_dspm_mne >> for MNE-Python's dSPM and << F.loc_family_n_sig_dspm >> for the study's. Among the joint-success comparisons they were << F.loc_family_n_sig_joint_ecd >> with the dipole fit and << F.loc_family_n_sig_joint_dspm >> with the study's dSPM, all favoring the OPM array. Of the << F.loc_family_n_sig >> with p < << F.wr_p_exploratory_threshold >>, << F.loc_family_n_sig_favour_opm >> favored an OPM array, << F.loc_family_n_sig_favour_zero >> had a zero median difference and << F.loc_family_n_sig_favour_squid >> favored Neuromag. Of the same << F.loc_family_n_sig >>, << F.loc_family_n_sig_80nam >> concerned mostly undetected << F.loc_strength_low_nam >>-nAm sources, and the two dSPM implementations share their events. A Bonferroni correction within anatomy and array (threshold << F.wr_locfig_bonferroni_threshold >>, the << F.wr_locfig_family_per_anatomy_and_array >> comparisons of one anatomy and OPM array) left << F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_20|words >> comparisons<% if F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_20 == F.wr_locfig_n_p_below_bonferroni %>, all error differences<% endif %>. << F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_20_n_80nam|words|capitalize >> of them were at << F.loc_strength_low_nam >> nAm, where most sources go undetected, and no joint-success comparison survived a correction. A correction over all << F.loc_family_n >> left <% if F.loc_survivors_bonferroni_all ==