\subsection{Head motion}\label{sec:S7.4}

Head motion and slippage of the OPM cap were bounded rather than simulated in time, on the adult and the << F.g3b_infant2yr_age_months >>- and << F.g3b_infant12mo_age_months >>-month templates at top contact. The head was displaced in the fixed helmet by up to << F.mot_translation_largest_mm >> mm or rotated about the head origin. The dense OPM cap was rotated on the head by up to << F.mot_slip_largest_deg >>°, lifting sensors that would enter the scalp. Each case was evaluated with the matched filter of the reference geometry (uncompensated) and with the displaced geometry known. A sustained << F.mot_translation_largest_mm >>-mm drop in the fixed helmet cost Neuromag << F.mot_squid_down10mm_mismatched_loss_db_range >> dB uncompensated and << F.mot_squid_down10mm_known_loss_db_range >> dB with the displaced geometry known. The latter is comparable to an uncompensated << F.mot_slip_largest_deg >>° slip of the OPM cap (<< F.mot_opm_slip3deg_mismatched_loss_db_range >> dB). A << F.mot_tc_duration_s >>-s time course of exact rigid motion checked the field-artifact model only; motion in the spike simulations, and its interaction with detection thresholds, was not simulated.

