Both spike runs used the fixed helmet and the modeled noise only. The spike study therefore does not show that fit causes a detection benefit in children, or how detection would fare under the noise-model alternatives of Section~\ref{sec:S3}. The pre-specified run also does not test the deeper bands, localization or a covariance mismatch of the detector. Its detector remains idealized in the ways named in the main text (Sections 2.5 and 4.4), and the mismatch variant is one declared departure, not a model of clinical review.
